WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
A camera on a tripod stands in a field.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.720
Its label reads: narrator.

3
00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:09.760
It zooms in close: a cheek, a red ribbon.

4
00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:13.800
Then it pulls far back, to
a valley under the stars.

5
00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:18.100
And then the camera
speaks: "Poor wounded name!

6
00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.920
My bosom as a bed shall lodge thee."

7
00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:22.340
It defends her.

8
00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:23.860
It stares at her.

9
00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.580
Can one narrator really do both?

10
00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.430
In this mission, you'll
track how the narrator moves,

11
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.570
from close-up to essay.

12
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.150
You'll read a scene
where a man watches Tess,

13
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.090
and ask who else is looking.

14
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:40.160
And you'll weigh readers
from 1891 to 1984,

15
00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:43.290
and test what each one
sees in this narrator.

16
00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:46.940
Your mission: decide whether
the narrator can do both.
